:"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Anita Hill","confidence":0.82}],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"Although the exact events between Clarence Thomas and Anita Hill may be unknowable, Brock argues that much about Anita Hill can be established that contradicts her public image and raises serious doubts about her credibility.","confidence":0.62},"academicOrientation":{"score":25,"confidence":0.5},"profileConfidence":0.78,"lowerConfidenceCandidates":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Clarence Thomas","confidence":0.55}]},"model":"gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"d46768e5c42d6a078fb5cf5fcc8881d6fb56b105f8493cac0a48220f538abf4c","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"primarySubject":"Gender & Sexuality","secondarySubjects":["Politics & Government","Society & Culture"],"confidence":"high","rationale":"The book primarily addresses the implications of sexual harassment within the political sphere, with a focus on the case of Anita Hill, thereby situating it firmly within Gender & Sexuality while also touching on Politics & Government and Society & Culture.","method":"llm","model":"gpt-4o-mini","reviewStatus":"generated","inputHash":"c983114c093f93d349dab781f34ec7549a5e43eaf6ccd4e268a91c313df7285f","summary":"More than a year and a half after the dramatic confrontation between Clarence Thomas and Anita Hill, opinions remain sharply divided on which one was telling the truth, and on the episode's significance and meaning for American society. Opinion polls conducted on the first anniversary of the hearings showed that public sentiment in Thomas' favor had weakened, while Anita Hill has become a national celebrity, a heroine credited with putting sexual harassment on the national agenda and thus a symbol of the feminist and civil rights movements who is said to have inspired a political \"year of the woman.\". The press has characterized the Hill-Thomas confrontation as an impenetrable mystery whose truth can never be known - an American version of Rashomon. But journalist David Brock dissents from this conclusion. His investigation shows that while there may indeed be no way of knowing exactly what transpired between Thomas and Hill, a great many things can be known about Anita Hill that were not previously disclosed which sharply contradict her public image and raise serious doubts about her credibility. Brock corrects numerous misconceptions and introduces new factual evidence to answer many questions left open by a notably uninquisitive national press.","publicationYear":1993,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Sexual harassment of women","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-real-anita-hill-david-brock"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Judges","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-real-anita-hill-david-brock"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Selection and appointment","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-real-anita-hill-david-brock"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"United States","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-real-anita-hill-david-brock"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"United States. Supreme Court","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-real-anita-hill-david-brock"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"New York Times reviewed","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-real-anita-hill-david-brock"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Hill, anita, 1956-","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-real-anita-hill-david-brock"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Thomas, clarence, 1948-","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-real-anita-hill-david-brock"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library